# Targets to remove from the destination on every `chezmoi apply`.
#
# These automation scripts moved from ~/.local/bin/ to ~/.local/bin/ai-tools/.
# chezmoi no longer manages the old flat paths, so it leaves them orphaned on
# disk; list them here so the pre-move copies are removed on hosts that already
# deployed them. Idempotent — removing an absent path is a no-op.
.local/bin/log-bash.sh
.local/bin/log-thinking.sh
.local/bin/compress-old-cache
.local/bin/claude-cache-stats
.local/bin/aws-mcp-server

# These three now ship from the flake (pkgs/, via localPackagesOverlay) instead
# of ~/.local/bin. That directory precedes ~/.nix-profile/bin on PATH, so a
# leftover copy would silently shadow the Nix one forever — technitium-dash was
# deployed here by chezmoi, wordgen and gopwgen by their old `task deploy`.
# Removing an absent path is a no-op, so this is safe on hosts that never had them.
.local/bin/technitium-dash
.local/bin/wordgen
.local/bin/gopwgen

# Their source checkouts, too. Both upstream repos were deleted when the
# sources moved into pkgs/, so the externals that cloned them failed on every
# apply; the external entries are gone and these leftover clones are dead
# weight. Content is preserved in pkgs/wordgen and pkgs/gopwgen.
.local/src/wordgen
.local/src/gopwgen
